# ============================================================================
# THE ROOT BUILD CONTEXT FILTER. THIS FILE IS LOAD-BEARING.
# ============================================================================
#
# docker-compose.yml builds `backend` and `sync` with `context: .`, so this is
# the .dockerignore Docker actually reads for both. It used to be inert -- every
# context was a subdirectory and this file was kept only as a sketch of what the
# next change would need. That change is here; it is now the only thing between
# a build and the entire repository.
#
# What sits at the root of this context:
#   .env, .credentials   real secrets on a developer machine and on the server
#   data/                on production, a SYMLINK to 2.4 TB of mirror data
#   .git/                every version of every file, including deleted ones
#   frontend/            the site, plus 13 self-hosted woff2 font files
#   nginx/, scripts/     config and shell, needed by no Python image
#   tests/               run from a checkout in CI, never inside an image
#
# DENY-BY-DEFAULT, NOT ALLOW-BY-DEFAULT
# -------------------------------------
# The first line excludes everything; the `!` lines re-admit exactly the two
# subtrees that a COPY reads. That ordering matters -- Docker applies patterns
# in order and the LAST match wins, so the re-exclusions at the bottom must stay
# below the `!` lines.
#
# The point of the inversion is what happens to a directory nobody has thought
# of yet. With a denylist, a new top-level `terraform/` or `backups/` is shipped
# into both images the day it is created and nothing says so. With this, it is
# excluded until someone adds a `!` line on purpose.
#
# PATTERNS DO NOT CROSS `/`
# -------------------------
# `*` compiles to `[^/]*`, so the leading `*` matches top-level entries only --
# which is exactly why `!backend` can then re-admit the whole backend/ subtree.
# For the same reason anything that can appear at ANY depth needs the `**/`
# prefix: `__pycache__` alone would not match `backend/app/api/__pycache__`.
# Verified below, not assumed -- see the CI job `docker-build`, which plants
# canary files and fails if any of them reaches a layer.
#
# THE SECOND LOCK
# ---------------
# This file is not the only defence, on purpose. backend/Dockerfile and
# sync/Dockerfile scope every COPY to `backend/` or `sync/`, so a hole here
# costs build time and cache churn but still cannot put a repo-root secret in a
# layer. Do not replace either COPY with `COPY . .`.
#
# ADDING THE SHARED MODELS PACKAGE
# --------------------------------
# Add `!shared` under the `!` block below and one scoped COPY line to each
# Dockerfile. Nothing else.
#
# NOT USED BY EVERY BUILD. The `rsync` service still builds from ./rsync, and
# Docker reads .dockerignore from the root of the build context -- so for that
# service this file does not apply.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Deny everything.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Re-admit only the subtrees a COPY reads.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!backend
!sync

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Re-exclude what must never ship, even from inside those subtrees.
#    These MUST stay below the `!` lines: last match wins.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Build recipes: the image does not need the instructions for building itself.
backend/Dockerfile
sync/Dockerfile
**/.dockerignore

# Secrets and local state. None of these are committed, and the COPY scoping
# means a root-level .env cannot reach a layer anyway -- but a backend/.env
# created by hand during debugging could, and this is what stops it.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.credentials
**/*.pem
**/*.key

# Python build/test artifacts
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
**/.venv
**/venv
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.coverage
**/.coverage.*
**/htmlcov
**/coverage.xml

# Tests do not run inside a runtime image; CI runs them from the checkout.
**/tests
**/test_*.py
**/conftest.py

# Editor / OS noise
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
**/*~
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/*.log
